  "title": "RTPS: Return end offset on failure",
  "description": "dissect_parameter_sequence is supposed to return an end offset.\nWhen it fails, return the end offset based on the passed in size\ninstead of returning zero, which can move the offset backwards.\n\nLuckily, most (all?) callers called proto_item_set_len afterwards,\nso instead of infinite loops there were a large number of\n\n ** (tshark:4093749) 12:08:48.186042 [Epan WARNING] -- Dissector bug, protocol RTPS, in packet 47484: epan/proto.c:7638: failed assertion \"length >= 0\" (text)\n\nfailed assertions from calling proto_item_set_len with a negative value.\nThose are now fixed.",
